1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:05,859
Why is the world's largest monolithic temple carved from the roof down instead of the ground up?

2
00:00:05,869 --> 00:00:12,304
At Ellora Cave 16, ancient Indian sculptors didn't assemble foundation stones upward.

3
00:00:12,304 --> 00:00:20,768
They started at the cliff summit, carving the temple spire first, then the ceiling, the pillars, and finally the courtyard floor!

4
00:00:20,768 --> 00:00:22,161
Why?

5
00:00:22,161 --> 00:00:27,343
Because in subtractive rock-cut architecture, the mountain was their scaffolding.

6
00:00:27,343 --> 00:00:34,166
As artisans chiseled downward into the basalt massif, they stood directly upon the bedrock they were sculpting.

7
00:00:34,166 --> 00:00:39,570
One wrong strike could shear a load-bearing lintel and collapse the overhead rock!

8
00:00:39,570 --> 00:00:46,054
Watch our full documentary linked below to see how ancient engineers carved Kailasa from above!

